Confirmed the Python side of this: `langchain_core` only knows the snake_case keys — the v1 content-block TypedDicts define `mime_type` (messages/content.py) and the v0-compat detection in messages/base.py keys off `source_type`. There is no camelCase normalization anywhere in `langchain_core`, so `mimeType`/`sourceType` blocks coming from the JS side fall through block detection and reach the provider untranslated, which is the 400 you're seeing.

Until the SDKs converge, a small boundary shim on the Python agent unblocks this:

```python
_KEY_MAP = {"mimeType": "mime_type", "sourceType": "source_type"}

def normalize_blocks(content: list) -> list:
    return [ 
        {_KEY_MAP.get(k, k): v for k, v in block.items()}
        if isinstance(block, dict)
        else block
        for block in content
    ]
```

applied to incoming message content before invoking the model.

Since the blocks are produced by Agent Chat UI / the LangGraph JS SDK, the durable fix probably needs to land there (emit the standard snake_case blocks) or in `langchain_core`'s block detection accepting both spellings — might be worth cross-filing so the right repo sees it.
